    {
      "seq": 18,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791896114651,
      "reason": "RegexTokenizer.encode_ordinary now memoises the token ids for each distinct regex chunk within a single call. Repeated chunks (common words, whitespace, punctuation) skip the BPE merge loop and reuse the ids already computed. The merges cannot change during a call, so the output is identical. The cache is local to the call, so there is no state to invalidate. Measured encode_ir ratio 0.9488 with identical equivalence outputs."
    }
